# vibe-trade V2 — three daily jobs + weekly report
# Timezone: Asia/Jerusalem (set host TZ or use timedatectl)
# Prereq: IB Gateway running on localhost:7497
#
# Install: crontab deploy/crontab.example
# Verify:  crontab -l
#
# RECORD TIMING — read before changing (corrected 2026-07-30):
# The US open is 16:30 Asia/Jerusalem (09:30 ET = 13:30 UTC; both zones are on
# summer time together for most of the year). Market orders placed at 16:00 fill
# AT the open, so their executions first appear in `ib.fills()` at ~16:30:0x.
#
# `record` reads `ib.fills()`. Running it at 16:25 — as this file said until
# 2026-07-30, and as ARCHITECTURE_V2.md still justified as "a 5-minute buffer
# before market open" — means it runs 5 minutes BEFORE any fill exists and
# records nothing. The live box has been on 16:35 all along, which is why it
# worked; the repo just never said so.
#
# 16:35 leaves 5 minutes of slack after the open. Reconcile at 23:30 back-fills
# anything record still misses (orphan BUY and orphan SELL recovery), so record
# is a fast-path, not the only path.
#
# DST caveat (corrected 2026-08-26 — the previous note here had the arithmetic
# backwards): Israel and the US flip DST on different dates. The US leaves DST
# the first Sunday of November and enters it the second Sunday of March;
# Israel leaves the last Sunday of October and enters the Friday before the
# last Sunday of March. In both gaps the offset between them is 6 hours
# instead of the usual 7, so the 09:30 ET US open lands at 15:30 Israel time —
# EARLIER, not later — which is roughly 14 trading days in March plus 5 in
# late October/early November each year (H-1, PROJECT_EVALUATION.md).
#
# During those windows submit (16:00) and preflight (15:50) both run AFTER
# the open, not before. Two things now guard against this in code rather than
# relying on getting cron's clock exactly right:
#   - submit refuses to evaluate a symbol whose last daily bar is today's US
#     date instead of a closed prior day (`_last_bar_is_closed`, H-1a) — so a
#     live intraday quote never gets traded as though it were a closed bar.
#   - record, at 16:35, may still be too early to see the open's fills in
#     that case; reconcile's 23:30 orphan-fill back-fill covers it either way.
# The cron *times* below are fixed Asia/Jerusalem clock times and do not
# themselves shift with the mismatch (H-1b). This is now fixed a different
# way: Ubuntu's default `cron` package ignores TZ/CRON_TZ for scheduling
# purposes (only passes it to the spawned process -- confirmed against
# `/usr/share/doc/cron/FEATURES`), so per-line timezones aren't possible here.
# `deploy/systemd/` replaces these four job lines with systemd timers whose
# `OnCalendar=` is anchored directly to America/New_York and tracks each DST
# transition correctly with zero manual adjustment (verified with
# `systemd-analyze calendar` across the actual Oct/Nov 2026 mismatch window).
# See deploy/systemd/README.md to migrate; this crontab keeps working as a
# fallback in the meantime and the code-level guards (H-1a, H-4) cover the
# actual trading-safety risk either way.

# Holiday caveat (H-4, PROJECT_EVALUATION.md): `1-5` is weekdays only, with no
# US market-holiday awareness (~9 weekdays/year: New Year's, MLK Day, Presidents
# Day, Good Friday, Memorial Day, Juneteenth, July 4th, Labor Day, Thanksgiving,
# Christmas). Both preflight and submit now check the real NYSE calendar in
# code (`data/market_calendar.py`) and skip cleanly on a non-trading day, so a
# holiday firing here is a safe no-op rather than the old failure mode: BUY
# day-orders left working overnight, which made the *next* session's
# double-run guard abort the whole day, exits included.
#
# Preflight — 10 minutes before submit. Verifies IB Gateway is up and logged in,
# the universe loads, and a strategy is enabled. Read-only. Telegrams on success
# AND failure, so silence (rather than a red message) is what should worry you.
# 10 minutes is enough to `systemctl restart ib-gateway` and re-run before 16:00.
# See ibgateway/README.md for the systemd + IBC setup that makes this rarely fire.
50 15 * * 1-5  cd /opt/vibe-trade/deploy && docker compose run --rm preflight >> ./logs/cron.log 2>&1

00 16 * * 1-5  cd /opt/vibe-trade/deploy && docker compose run --rm submit   >> ./logs/cron.log 2>&1
35 16 * * 1-5  cd /opt/vibe-trade/deploy && docker compose run --rm record   >> ./logs/cron.log 2>&1
30 23 * * 1-5  cd /opt/vibe-trade/deploy && docker compose run --rm reconcile >> ./logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Weekly report — Saturday 09:00. Renders reports/<date>-weekly.png + Telegram.
00 09 * * 6    cd /opt/vibe-trade/deploy && docker compose run --rm report-weekly >> ./logs/cron.log 2>&1

# Daily DB backup — 23:45, after reconcile is done. Keeps 14 days. Runs all
# 7 days/week, not just weekdays: the previous `1-5` schedule meant a
# Saturday disk failure could lose Friday's entire trading day with no
# backup to restore from (PROJECT_EVALUATION.md).
#
# Uses SQLite's online `.backup` (safe mid-write/WAL) + integrity_check +
# a `.sha256` sidecar, not a plain `cp` -- a torn/mid-write copy would pass
# `cp` silently and sit for up to 14 days until `integrity_check` (which
# nothing ran) would have caught it. The `.sha256` sidecar is also what
# docs/playbooks/data-recovery.md's restore procedure actually needs to run
# `sha256sum -c` against; the old `cp`-based backup never wrote one.
# See scripts/nightly_backup.py. Runs inside bare python:3.11-slim (sqlite3
# is stdlib) -- no apk/apt install step, so no network dependency at 23:45.
45 23 * * *    docker run --rm -v deploy_vibe-data:/data:ro -v /opt/vibe-trade/backups:/backup -v /opt/vibe-trade/scripts:/scripts:ro python:3.11-slim@sha256:be1575ed968de893bd54f4c56315ff7c4736ce522c1bca08fd521731aafc0d76 python /scripts/nightly_backup.py --db /data/vibe_trade.db --out /backup --keep-days 14 >> /opt/vibe-trade/deploy/logs/cron.log 2>&1
